{"source":"github","project_id":"lltm","target":"mlverse/lltm","id":"pr/5","ref":5,"title":"Error handling","description":"Handle exceptions raised from C++ in the `csrc` directory. \r\nExceptions are not safe if raised from code compiled in MSVC that interface with Rcpp et al compiled with MinGW. Thus we need to handle them to make sure no function in the C api raises C++ exceptions.\r\n\r\nInstead we catch the exceptions and save them into a pointer that can then be checked from Rcpp and we re-raise the exception if needed.","published_at":"2022-01-17T21:48:05Z","updated_at":"2022-01-19T12:27:14Z","url":"https://github.com/mlverse/lltm/pull/5","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"dfalbel","merged_at":"2022-01-19T12:27:14Z","state":"MERGED"}}
